    q: 'How do EU boot sizes convert to US sizes?',
    a: 'When translating EU boot size to US (such as hiking boots, winter insulated footwear, or chelsea boots), standard conversion rules apply, but shoemakers strongly recommend sizing up by a half or full European size. This accounts for thicker winter socks and prevents toe bruising on downhill inclines.'
